{-
   Every way of claiming a compiler role wrongly - `compiler/intrinsic/role.h`.

   One fixture rather than four, because they are one mechanism seen from four sides and reading
   them together is what shows that: the role has to exist, it has to be written on the kind of
   declaration the row wants, one declaration has to fill it, and a form that can fill nothing has
   to say so rather than accept the attribute and do nothing with it.

   All four are answerable from the attribute and the declaration's own form, which is why they are
   one fixture: `bindRole` reports every one of them while the declarations are being read, and
   `resolveProgram` stops there. The checks that need a *finished* signature run after that point,
   so an intrinsic's shape is `Reject.Shape.yana` beside this.

   A **supplied** global's four storage rules used to be `Reject.Supplied.yana` and no longer have a
   fixture. `lib/` claims all seven rows of `supplied.def`, so a program's claim is refused here as
   a duplicate before `checkSuppliedGlobal` is reached, and a golden that got past that would carry
   the library's own line numbers in it. `prelude/` was the only library that left a supplied role
   unclaimed, and it is gone (J21).
-}

-- A role no table has. The message lists every role the compiler knows, built from the tables rather
-- than written out, so a role added anywhere is in it.
@builtin(mulHi)
fn misspelled(a: I64, b: I64) -> I64

-- The kind of declaration the row wants. `drop` is a class, and this is not.
@builtin(drop)
fn notAClass(x: I32) -> I32 = x

-- Two declarations claiming one role. Refused rather than taken, because there is one slot and
-- taking the last would make which one the compiler reached depend on declaration order. A **host**
-- role, because those are the only ones `lib/` leaves unclaimed on a native build - a role the
-- library fills is one this file cannot claim even once, and `mulHigh` used to stand here until it
-- did.
@builtin(hostGrow)
fn growOne(items: %a, wide: Size) -> %a

@builtin(hostGrow)
fn growTwo(items: %a, wide: Size) -> %a

-- And a declaration form that fills no role at all.
data Box {value: I32}

@builtin(drop)
instance Drop(Box):
    fn drop(->value: Box): return

fn main() -> I32 = 0
